    "terrainName": "basic-desert",
    "description": "What: night shortens sight (CE-4035 G-10; PerceptionWeather S2-1n: range x the light factor, floor 0.25), on basic-desert at 00:30 local (22:30 UTC), clear sky. Two identical pairs: 'Observer Clear' at (0, 0) and 'Observer Second' at (0, 300) (riflemen, sight 150 m, holding); 'Target Clear' and 'Target Second' (insurgents) walk west to them from 220 m at 1.4 m/s. Judge: each observer first SEES his target well inside 150 m — about 40 m (150 x 0.25). Compare: ua-weather-sensing (the same pairs by day, one in fog). Fail: a target seen beyond 75 m. Note: thermal sights are not in the catalogue yet (CE-4035 G-10 open). Check: python3 scripts/utility-demo-check.py --launch ua-night-sensing"
